.TH "YAMLR-MANUAL" "1" "March 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBThe Terminal User Guide & Reference\fR
.PP
The \fBmanual\fR command renders high-fidelity documentation directly in your terminal. This allows for a 100% offline-first experience where you never have to leave the shell to master the engine.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
yamlr manual [TOPIC]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **The Big Book**: Running \fByamlr manual\fR with no arguments opens the full **Yamlr User Guide**.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Targeted Reference**: Pass a command name (e.g., \fBscan\fR, \fBheal\fR, \fBrules\fR) to view the specific manual for that subcommand.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Specialized Topics**:
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBconfig\fR: Opens the full **Yamlr Configuration Guide** (\fBCONFIGURATION.md\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Rich Rendering**: Uses the engine's internal markdown processor for a premium, formatted reading experience.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Offline-First**: Bundled directly into the binary; no internet connection required.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
\fBOpen the main User Guide:\fR
.PP
.nf
.RS
yamlr manual
.RE
.fi
\fBView the Scan command manual:\fR
.PP
.nf
.RS
yamlr manual scan
.RE
.fi
\fBView the Configuration Guide:\fR
.PP
.nf
.RS
yamlr manual config
.RE
.fi
